Package: swbrd-ext-echo
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Evan Brass <brassevan@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: swbrd-common (>= @COMPAT@), swbrd-dtls-proxy (>= @COMPAT@), systemd, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54), libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1
Homepage: https://github.com/evan-brass/swbrd
Description: Example switchboard extension that echoes
 Serves the echo.v1 datachannel protocol: greets the peer by the id derived
 from their certificate, then sends back whatever they send.  Useful as a
 reachability check for the whole path -- DTLS termination, association rejoin,
 and channel dispatch -- and as the smallest worked example of the extension
 protocol.
 .
 Built for one private host and not fit for redistribution; see
 /usr/share/doc/swbrd-ext-echo/copyright.
